What is the mean number of books read per student?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2.1$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2.5$"},{"key":"D","text":"$7$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'The sum of all values is $0(2) + 1(5) + 2(6) + 3(4) + 4(2) + 5(1) = 0 + 5 + 12 + 12 + 8 + 5 = 42$. Dividing by the total number of students: $42/20 = 2.1$. The value $2$ results from finding the median instead of the mean (the 10th and 11th values in sorted order are both $2$, so the median is $2$). The value $2.5$ results from averaging the possible book counts without using frequencies: $(0 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5)/6 = 15/6 = 2.5$. The value $7$ results from dividing the weighted sum by the number of categories rather than the total frequency: $42/6 = 7$.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"equation_setup_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 75, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);






















